Browsh's embedded unsigned extension is installed for the current browser
session, using Marionette's supported temporary add-on installation API.
Firefox ESR 140's Addon:Install handler accepts `temporary` and delegates to
AddonManager.installTemporaryAddon; this path does not require signing.

Firefox ESR 140 also requires explicit system access for chrome-context
Marionette scripts and exports Preferences as an ES module rather than JSM.

The temporary archive must retain an .xpi extension.  Firefox's XPIProvider
isXPI classifier treats a filename without .xpi/.zip as an unpacked add-on,
causing bootstrap to search the parent directory for manifest.json.

Marionette commands are length-framed request/response exchanges.  Consume
the greeting and each matching response before issuing dependent commands,
so session startup finishes before add-on and preference operations.

Source API references (Firefox 140 ESR release):
https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/FIREFOX_140_0esr_RELEASE/remote/marionette/driver.sys.mjs
https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/FIREFOX_140_0esr_RELEASE/remote/shared/Addon.sys.mjs
https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/FIREFOX_140_0esr_RELEASE/toolkit/modules/Preferences.sys.mjs
https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/FIREFOX_140_0esr_RELEASE/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIProvider.sys.mjs

